  <h1>Introduction to Java</h1>

  <p>Java is a popular programming language that was created in 1995.</p>
  <p>It is owned by Oracle, and more than 3 billion devices run Java.</p>

  <p><strong>Java is used for:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Mobile applications (especially Android apps)</li>
    <li>Desktop applications</li>
    <li>Web applications</li>
    <li>Web servers and application servers</li>
    <li>Games</li>
    <li>Database connections</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Why Use Java?</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Works on all platforms (Windows, Mac, Linux, etc.)</li>
    <li>Popular and widely supported</li>
    <li>Easy to learn and open-source</li>
    <li>Secure, fast, and powerful</li>
    <li>Supports Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Simple Java Code:</strong></p>
  <pre><code>
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
  </code></pre>

